{"Django ORM does not support negative slicing - Django QuerySets explicitly prohibit negative indexing and will raise AssertionError when a negative start_offset is passed as a slice index, causing 500 errors when clients craft cursors with negative offset values": 0.9568457007408142, "get_item_key will raise TypeError on datetime fields - math.floor() and math.ceil() require a real number but AuditLogEntry.datetime returns a datetime.datetime object, not a float, causing TypeError when processing results": 0.9218233227729797, "organization_context.member can be None - RpcUserOrganizationContext.member is typed as Optional[RpcOrganizationMember] and accessing .has_global_access without a None guard causes AttributeError for superusers without explicit org membership": 0.9073418974876404, "Hard-coded eviction limit (1000) is inconsistent with configurable max_segment_spans - The Lua script hard-codes 1000 as the cap while SpansBuffer accepts max_segment_spans as a constructor parameter, making runtime tuning impossible without changing source": 0.7427135705947876, "Silent eviction drops spans without any logging or metrics - The Lua eviction silently removes individual spans with no observability, unlike the previous Python-side guard that emitted metrics and logger.error": 0.8344041705131531, "zpopmin removes oldest-ending spans which may include parent/root spans - Evicting spans with smallest end_timestamp_precise (oldest-ending spans) creates incomplete trace trees that are harder to debug than dropping entire over-sized segments": 0.7136538028717041, "max_segment_spans is now a dead parameter on SpansBuffer - The Python-side span-count guard was removed but max_segment_spans is still accepted as a constructor parameter and stored but never used anywhere in the class": 0.8166929483413696}